{"step_index":280,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T06:41:04Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-09-01T06:37:40Z sender=3a379be0-df21-4555-9015-d3353de8b2ba priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Here is the Python script:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport math\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n# Directory setup\noutput_dir = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\stickman_master_asset\"\nos.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nwidth, height = 1920, 1080\nbg_color = \"#00FF00\" # Neon green\n\ndef draw_blackboard(draw):\n    # Board outer frame\n    board_rect = [(200, 100), (1400, 700)]\n    draw.rectangle(board_rect, fill=\"#2c3e50\", outline=\"#8B4513\", width=20)\n    # Chalk tray\n    draw.rectangle([(180, 700), (1420, 730)], fill=\"#8B4513\")\n    \ndef draw_happy_face(draw, cx, cy, radius):\n    # Head\n    draw.ellipse([(cx-radius, cy-radius), (cx+radius, cy+radius)], fill=\"white\", outline=\"black\", width=5)\n    # Eyes\n    eye_radius = 5\n    draw.ellipse([(cx-20-eye_radius, cy-15-eye_radius), (cx-20+eye_radius, cy-15+eye_radius)], fill=\"black\")\n    draw.ellipse([(cx+20-eye_radius, cy-15-eye_radius), (cx+20+eye_radius, cy-15+eye_radius)], fill=\"black\")\n    # Happy mouth\n    bbox = [(cx-25, cy-10), (cx+25, cy+30)]\n    draw.arc(bbox, start=0, end=180, fill=\"black\", width=5)\n\ndef draw_stickman(draw, frame_idx, total_frames):\n    # Base coordinates\n    head_x, head_y = 1600, 450\n    head_r = 60\n    \n    # Body\n    neck_y = head_y + head_r\n    pelvis_y = neck_y + 250\n    draw.line([(head_x, neck_y), (head_x, pelvis_y)], fill=\"black\", width=10)\n    \n    # Legs\n    left_foot = (head_x - 80, pelvis_y + 250)\n    right_foot = (head_x + 80, pelvis_y + 250)\n    draw.line([(head_x, pelvis_y), left_foot], fill=\"black\", width=10)\n    draw.line([(head_x, pelvis_y), right_foot], fill=\"black\", width=10)\n    \n    # Left Arm (hanging down)\n    shoulder_y = neck_y + 40\n    left_hand = (head_x + 100, shoulder_y + 150)\n    draw.line([(head_x, shoulder_y), left_hand], fill=\"black\", width=10)\n    \n    # Right Arm (pointing at the board, animated)\n    # The animation will move the hand up and down slightly while pointing at the board.\n    # Frame index goes from 0 to 89\n    \n    # Angle calculation (smooth back and forth motion)\n    angle_offset = math.sin((frame_idx / total_frames) * 2 * math.pi) * 25 # degrees\n    \n    base_angle = -150 # pointing towards the board (left and up)\n    current_angle = base_angle + angle_offset\n    \n    arm_length = 220\n    rad = math.radians(current_angle)\n    right_hand_x = head_x + arm_length * math.cos(rad)\n    right_hand_y = shoulder_y + arm_length * math.sin(rad)\n    \n    draw.line([(head_x, shoulder_y), (right_hand_x, right_hand_y)], fill=\"black\", width=10)\n    \n    # Draw Head with happy face\n    draw_happy_face(draw, head_x, head_y, head_r)\n    \n\nfor i in range(90):\n    img = Image.new(\"RGB\", (width, height), bg_color)\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\n    \n    draw_blackboard(draw)\n    draw_stickman(draw, i, 90)\n    \n    # Save frame\n    frame_number = i + 1\n    filename = f\"frame_{frame_number:03d}.png\"\n    filepath = os.path.join(output_dir, filename)\n    img.save(filepath)\n\nprint(\"Finished generating frames.\")\n```\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
